 "id": "2026-11-11-russia-refineries-rationing",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Thirty percent of Russia's oil refining knocked out, sources say. Who feels it first?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Two industry sources told Reuters that Ukrainian drone strikes since late October have cut Russia's refining capacity by about thirty percent. Nine of thirty-five major refineries were disrupted. The regional governor says Kirishi, the second largest, caught fire on Monday."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Drivers feel it first. Euronews and Semafor report that Rosneft, Russia's biggest oil company, now caps fuel sales in several regions, at thirty litres per purchase in cities. It had eased rationing in October, during a pause in the strikes."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Overnight, the drones kept coming. The Leningrad governor says one hundred forty-six were downed, and a fire broke out at the Ust-Luga port on the Baltic. Lithuania and Latvia warned residents to shelter, reports say."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will Russia and Ukraine agree to stop energy strikes this winter? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
